==English==

===Etymology===
Imitative in both uses, the first being of snoring: compare {{m|en|zzz||sound of snoring}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/zɪz/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[nap]] or [[sleep]].
#* '''1973''', Kyril Bonfiglioli, ''Don't Point That Thing at Me'' (Penguin 2001, page 45)
#*: Then I had a little '''zizz''' until Martland telephoned.
# A buzzing or whizzing sound.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|es}}

# {{lb|en|informal|intransitive}} To take a nap.